Authorization and authentication boundaries:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/linux-pam/linux-pam/master/modules/pam_sepermit/pam_sepermit.8.xml
# pam_sepermit implements auth and account; matching users are denied unless
# SELinux is enforcing. Preserve required gates in either stack.
# Retain postlogin only after auditing actual auth contents. The default is
# session-only; with-ecryptfs adds password-dependent optional auth and is not
# supported. Do not edit authselect-generated password-auth/postlogin files.
# Preserve their account/session/password references. Recursively audit the
# auth flow before replacing credentials: pam_usertype/pam_localuser jumps
# cannot remain capable of skipping the burner. Mandatory U2F/smartcard,
# systemd-homed, custom auth modules, and unknown control flow fail closed.
# No claim that central password/MFA policy can be silently discarded.

